{"skill":{"slug":"financial-calculator","displayName":"Financial Calculator Pro"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770314147256,"changelog":"Initial release: Future Value, Present Value, Discount, Markup, Compound Interest calculators with interactive charts, tables, and year+month support. Includes CLI and beautiful web UI.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5802,"sha256":"bc0442cf441d2fd43e5ab2e19b50d0d728c9e024f82f86063ef259beba0b14fc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/calculator.html","size":46309,"sha256":"7d3eccfca3ef10105b70d22078a0f0ce8aa37d6d143ed012e49fead215220dd0","contentType":"text/html"},{"path":"references/formulas.md","size":4215,"sha256":"5df9d453dbbb37d0260d3b98516364a9aa92485fbe715e46d87153b3d7ece1d7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/calculate.py","size":8587,"sha256":"4618dfb8e207872c2bd3de3258bdbbaac43f0db88a86d6eb156e5d97d3889179","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/launch_ui.sh","size":572,"sha256":"b7fc5e339fe993b2f9b7011bcbda2d600227ddcc19a9982d23a1ebb9d280026d","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/web_ui.py","size":6750,"sha256":"2971ec9ab21ba92512b2c51dd7b377bda735721f039c51b9e3058e77279926ea","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2063,"sha256":"bec062c719350fe7b9ff8c6255bdb5b77f09bd4dfee1c08a9dd49644073dee50","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035409739,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"21b0c730e0c8b94563433554d7dab97c8d6a6c4772829d9433987ac395953b9b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/21b0c730e0c8b94563433554d7dab97c8d6a6c4772829d9433987ac395953b9b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\nSuspicious High-Entropy/Eval files: 3\n\nThe OpenClaw skill bundle provides a financial calculator with both CLI and web UI functionalities. Analysis of all files, including `SKILL.md`, `launch_ui.sh`, `calculate.py`, `web_ui.py`, and `calculator.html`, reveals no evidence of malicious intent. The `SKILL.md` contains only descriptive instructions and legitimate usage examples, without any prompt injection attempts. The shell script (`launch_ui.sh`) and Python code (`calculate.py`, `web_ui.py`) perform standard financial calculations, install a common dependency (Flask) into a virtual environment, and serve a local web UI. There are no signs of data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation. The skill's behavior is clearly aligned with its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161633217},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":41,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789035409739},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent financial calculator, but it needs Review because its web UI is under-scoped for a local tool and depends on mutable third-party code.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The documentation presents the UI as localhost, but the Flask server binds to 0.0.0.0 and exposes unauthenticated endpoints with unbounded year/rate inputs, making denial-of-service by other reachable network peers a concrete risk.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The launcher auto-creates a persistent venv and installs Flask without pinning versions or hashes, so first launch can download mutable Python dependency code from the configured package index.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are user-directed and do not contain prompt hijacking, hidden role changes, credential requests, or unrelated agent behavior. The UI does post entered values to same-origin Flask endpoints, which is expected for this design but not clearly disclosed in the page.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No system service, scheduled task, privilege escalation, credential use, or cross-session agent persistence was found. The only persistence observed is the disclosed local virtual environment under the skill directory.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts match the stated financial-calculator purpose: CLI functions, Flask API routes, web UI forms, charts, and formula references all focus on financial calculations. Extra annuity helper functions are related and documented in the formulas reference, though not emphasized in the main description.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable reviewing or mitigating the web UI risks. Prefer changing the server to bind to 127.0.0.1, adding input limits, pinning Python dependencies, and vendoring or integrity-pinning Chart.js before using it with sensitive financial data or on a shared network.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the web UI is present in the artifact, and the annuity functions are financial helpers documented in references/formulas.md rather than unrelated behavior.\n[SDI-2] expected: Accepted as a supply-chain concern: Chart.js is reasonable for chart rendering, but loading it from a CDN without integrity protection gives third-party JavaScript access to the calculator page.\n[SQP-3] expected: Low materiality for this security verdict: declaring html lang=\"en\" is not evidence of hidden or harmful behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Partly accepted: same-origin fetch calls are expected for the Flask UI, but users are not clearly told that entered financial values are sent to server-side endpoints.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: binding the Flask development server to all interfaces while accepting unbounded table/chart inputs is broader than needed for a local calculator and creates a realistic resource-exhaustion risk.\n[T08] expected: Accepted for scripts/launch_ui.sh: Flask is a legitimate dependency for the UI, but automatic unpinned installation during launch is an avoidable supply-chain risk.\n[T08] expected: Accepted for assets/calculator.html: Chart.js supports the stated chart feature, but the remote browser script is not protected by SRI or vendored locally.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035409739}}}}}